{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Progress at 90d57e392ba (session a85e3cd3).\n\nReproduced: with compact_all_cli/compact_cli replaced by a no-op returning 1, all 4 named tests PASSED (4 passed in 90.65s). With fsck_cli replaced the same way, test_fsck_quiet_when_in_sync PASSED; the 3 CLI-driven siblings failed correctly.\n\nFinding: test_dry_run_never_pushes and test_no_commit_never_pushes never reached the \"Nothing to do.\" early return their comment names. tests/conftest.py sets REBAR_COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS=0, so the backfill arm selects the fresh snapshot-less ticket whatever the 9999 threshold says: --dry-run took the \"would compact\" return, and --no-commit folded the ticket. Both tests now set a 1-hour horizon so nothing is selected. The fold-path --no-commit case stays covered by test_compact_sweep_handover.py::test_a_no_commit_sweep_pushes_nothing.\n\nAfter the change: under the seeded no-op all 5 strengthened tests FAIL; clean, the 3 touched files pass (41 passed). Behaviour mutations are caught too: _best_effort_push ignoring its flags fails both push tests; _sweep_should_yield always False fails the yield test (folded 4); a per-ticket walk inside _build_authorship_ledger fails the lock test.\n\nDiscovered: screaming-downy-kissingbug (test_a_sweep_with_nothing_selected_still_pushes passes with _best_effort_push as a no-op). Also closed sappy-overempty-rat as not_a_bug: an accidental placeholder create from this session."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793774663616151001,"uuid":"4b0f268e-6730-4b39-8aed-0fe6592d03fb"}